id: 6
hanzi: 评委
pinyin: píng wěi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: judge; member of a judging panel; evaluation committee member
  es: miembro del jurado; juez calificador; evaluador

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a person serving on a judging committee or jury for a contest or evaluation | persona que forma parte de un comité evaluador o jurado calificador | 担任评委 (serve as a judge)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在今晚的青年歌手大奖赛现场，著名音乐家担任主评委并对每位选手的表现给予了中肯点评。 | Zài jīnwǎn de qīngnián gēshǒu dàjiǎngsài xiànchǎng, zhùmíng yīnyuèjiā dānrèn zhǔ píngwěi bìng duì měi wèi xuǎnshǒu de biǎoxiàn jǐyǔ le zhòngkěn diǎnpíng. | At tonight's young singers competition, a renowned musician served as head judge and offered pertinent feedback on each contestant's performance. | En la gala de cantantes juveniles de esta noche, un destacado músico actuó como juez principal y brindó comentarios acertados sobre cada concursante.
  #2 | 科技创新基金评审委员会明确规定，与参评企业存在利益关联的专家必须主动申请回避评委职务。 | Kējì chuàngxīn jījīn píngshěn wěiyuánhuì míngquè guīdìng, yǔ cānpíng qǐyè cúnzài lìyì guānlián de zhuānjiā bìxū zhǔdòng shēnqǐng huíbì píngwěi zhíwù. | The Science and Technology Innovation Fund review committee expressly stipulates that experts with vested interests in participating firms must recuse themselves from serving as judges. | El comité de evaluación del fondo de innovación tecnológica estipula con claridad que los expertos con conflictos de interés con las empresas aspirantes deben abstenerse de integrar el jurado.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  担任评委 | serve as a judge
  评委会主席 | jury president / head of judging panel
  特邀评委 | guest judge
  专业评委 | professional juror
  大众评委 | popular/audience juror
  评委打分 | judges' scoring

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  评头品足 | píng tóu pǐn zú | find fault with; make hypercritical comments
  委曲求全 | wěi qū qiú quán | compromise for the sake of the general interest
  虚与委蛇 | xū yǔ wēi yí | deal with someone insincerely; play along politely
  评功摆好 | píng gōng bǎi hǎo | sing praises of one's own contributions

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  评 | píng | evaluate; judge; criticize; discuss | evaluar; juzgar; criticar; comentar | 讠 | speech | 讠 (speech, uttering verdicts) | 平 (píng, level/fair) | 7 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound combining speech (讠) with fairness/balance (平), conveying speaking impartial truth. | Words spoken (讠) across a level balance scale (平) represent fair judicial appraisal. | Palabras expresadas (讠) sobre una balanza equilibrada (平) representan un juicio imparcial. | 35 | IVMF | 評
  委 | wěi | entrust; appoint; committee; indirect | encomendar; encargar; comité; indirecto | 女 | woman | 女 (woman / yielding compliance) | 禾 (grain / resource managed) | 8 | 上下结构 | Depicts grain (禾) entrusted to a household manager (女), evolving to mean delegation of authority. | Harvested sheaves of grain (禾) are entrusted to the capable hands of a matriarch (女) to manage. | Las gavillas de trigo (禾) se encomiendan al cuidado prudente de una mujer (女) para su gestión. | 214 | HDV | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: One who speaks with fair words (评) and is entrusted with authority (委) sits as a respected judge.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Quien emite juicios equilibrados (评) y recibe la confianza encomendada (委) actúa como juez en el tribunal.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In Chinese governance, 'píng' denotes level-headed appraisal without bias, while 'wěi' (abbreviation of 委员会委员) conveys delegated communal trust; together, a 评委 is a guardian of meritocratic fairness.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: 35-214 pitch contour. The rising tone of píng leads smoothly into the dipping tone of wěi. In fluent conversation, wěi often stays in a low dipping contour (21) when followed by further syllables.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    许 | xǔ | allow; praise | Right side is 午 (noon) rather than 平 (level)
    订 | dìng | order; book | Right side is 丁 rather than 平
    季 | jì | season; quarter | Features 禾 over 子 (child) instead of 女 (woman)
    秀 | xiù | elegant; show | Features 禾 over 乃 instead of 女
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    平 | píng | level; fair; phonetic root of 评
    论 | lùn | discuss; evaluate in the speech radical family
    托 | tuō | entrust; related in semantic delegation to 委
    员 | yuán | member; official roster

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 评委 denotes an officially appointed adjudicator or committee member tasked with assessing contest submissions and awarding scores.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 评委 vs. 裁判 | cáipàn | 裁判 is primarily used in athletic events and legal arbitrations for enforcing rules, whereas 评委 adjudicates artistic, academic, or competitive talent performances.
    2 | 评委 vs. 专家 | zhuānjiā | 专家 is an expert possessing domain mastery in a field, who may or may not act as a 评委 in a specific judging panel.
    3 | 评委 vs. 考官 | kǎoguān | 考官 specifically refers to an examiner overseeing formal aptitude or academic examinations, whereas 评委 ranks contestants in competitive venues.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 艺术比赛的舞台不仅见证选手的汗水，更考验评委的眼光。面对风格各异的参赛作品，优秀的评委总能剥离华丽的表象，发现直击心灵的灵性表达。中肯的评语如同一束光，指引着青年探索者前行的方向。 | Yìshù bǐsài de wǔtái bùjǐn jiànzhèng xuǎnshǒu de hànshuǐ, gèng kǎoyàn píngwěi de yǎnguāng. Miànduì fēnggé gèyì de cānsài zuòpǐn, yōuxiù de píngwěi zǒng néng bōlí huálì de biǎoxiàng, fāxiàn zhíjī xīnlíng de língxìng biǎodá. Zhòngkěn de píngyǔ rútóng yí shù guāng, zhǐyǐn zhe qīngnián tànsuǒzhě qiánxíng de fāngxiàng. | The stage of an arts contest tests not only contestants' sweat but judges' discernment. Confronting diverse works, outstanding judges see through superficial gloss to spot genuine soul. Pertinent commentary serves as a beacon lighting the path of young creators. | El escenario de un certamen artístico pone a prueba la mirada del jurado tanto como el esfuerzo de los participantes. Ante obras variadas, los jurados perspicaces trascienden la superficie para valorar la autenticidad emocional, guiando a los jóvenes creadores.
  #2 | 在现代科技成果评估体系中，评委团队的跨学科构成已成为确保评审客观性的制度基石。来自产业界与学术界的资深评委共同参与答辩，从学术前沿价值与产业转化可行性双重视角，严格审核每一项申报成果。 | Zài xiàndài kējì chéngguǒ pínggū tǐxì zhōng, píngwěi tuánduì de kuà xuékē gòuchéng yǐ chéngwéi quèbǎo píngshěn kèguānxìng de zhìdù jīshí. Lázì chǎnyèjiè yǔ xuéshùjiè de zīshēn píngwěi gòngtóng cānyù dábbiàn, cóng xuéshù qiányán jiàzhí yǔ chǎnyè zhuǎnhuà kěxíngxìng shuāngzhòng shìjiǎo, yángé shěnhé měi yí xiàng shēnbào chéngguǒ. | In modern scientific evaluation systems, the interdisciplinary composition of judging panels forms an institutional bedrock for objectivity. Senior jurors from industry and academia participate jointly in defenses, evaluating innovations through academic frontiers and market feasibility. | En la evaluación científica contemporánea, la integración interdisciplinaria del jurado constituye la base de la objetividad institucional. Jueces veteranos del sector industrial y académico evalúan conjuntamente los proyectos desde la validez teórica y su viabilidad productiva.
